        "original_id": "6b8035b7-8baa-5d59-adf8-8df2df010713",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Revolt of the Beavers, Mother Goose\n- Organizations: Federal Theater Project\n- People: Oscar Saul, Louis Lantz, Arthur Rackham\n- Places: Adelphi Theatre, New York City, United Kingdom\n- Concepts: Marxism a la Mother Goose, fairy tales, nursery rhymes, Christmas pantomime\n\nFacts:\n- Mother Goose is the imaginary author associated with a collection of fairy tales and nursery rhymes often published as \"Old Mother Goose's Rhymes.\"\n- In 1913, Arthur Rackham illustrated \"Old Mother Goose's Rhymes.\"\n- Revolt of the Beavers was a children's play presented by the Federal Theater Project and written by Oscar Saul and Louis Lantz.\n- Revolt of the Beavers ran at the Adelphi Theatre in New York City from May 20, 1937, to June 19, 1937.\n- One critic described Revolt of the Beavers as \"Marxism a la Mother Goose.\"\n- A Christmas pantomime called \"Mother Goose\" is often performed in the United Kingdom.",
